Package: psymp3
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: audio player with FFT spectrum visualization
 PsyMP3 is a cross-platform audio player built around a real-time FFT
 spectrum analyzer and a Windows 3.x-styled in-application window system.
 .
 It decodes MP3, MP2, FLAC, Ogg Vorbis, Opus, Speex, AAC, ALAC, WAV
 (PCM, A-law, mu-law and G.722) and raw streams, using bundled decoders
 for Vorbis (stb_vorbis), MP3 (minimp3), MP2 (kjmp2) and ALAC so the
 codec set does not vary with what the system happens to provide.
 .
 Playback integrates with the desktop through MPRIS, scrobbles to
 Last.fm, and can publish now-playing state to Discord.
